<article class="env-lemma" id="0671">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0671">Lemma <span data-tag="0671">15.82.9</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a finite type ring map. Let $0 \to M' \to M \to M'' \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of $A$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $M', M''$ are finitely presented relative to $R$, then so is $M$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $M'$ is a finite type $A$-module and $M$ is finitely presented relative to $R$, then $M''$ is finitely presented relative to $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0519" data-tag="0519">10.5.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>